​

Despite the complicated external envrionment that hampered smooth project implementation, the partners managed to execute the project within the limits of what was realistically possible. They performed as much as they could and the following 5 major achievements have been the results of their continued efforts:

1. An “ONEF Model” for employment projection

2. An ONEF Gender Plan

3. Strengthened capacities of ONEF staff in:

 Statistical analysis

 Gender

 Strategic Planning and Results-Based Management

4. Broadened and strengthened partnership (CINOP, RAOEF, national structures)

5. Equipment for remote work

These deliverables available are very relevant and have already had a positive impact on ONEF and its operations. We can mention the following noticeable positive effects thanks to the project's performance:

 Increased visibility of ONEF in Mali and in the sub-region;

 Increasing number of requests for ONEF by external partners for the execution of paid consultations;

 A gender analysis of the labor market carried out;

 Systematic consideration of gender in all aspects of ONEF's life;

 Active participation of ONEF in the workshop on political dialogue on the process of integrating the gender dimension in the post-Covid-19 recovery;

 Qualitative leap in the individual work of certain agents thanks to the new knowledge and skills acquired;

 Use of remote work as needed.
